course: dictionary
lesson: 9637
title: Stumpy: short and thick
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Stumpy» means short and thick, like a tree stump. Read the words around it to check. A stumpy tail is not long and thin, and a stumpy pencil is a short, chunky one.
explain: The clues often tell you the meaning. «Tortoises have domed shells and stumpy legs, while water turtles have flatter shells and webbed feet or flippers.» The word while shows a contrast, so tortoise legs must be different from flippers: short and thick.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put in "short and thick" and see if it still makes sense. It does, so you can be sure.
fact: Stumpy means short and thick, like a tree stump.
fact: Stumpy can describe animals, plants, people's legs or pencils.
fact: Tortoises have «stumpy legs» and heavy, domed shells.
fact: Tardigrades, or water bears, have 8 «stumpy legs» with claws that grip moss and soil.
fact: The forms are stumpy, stumpier and stumpiest: stumpier means more short and thick, and stumpiest means the most.
exercise: «The tortoise walked slowly on its stumpy legs.» What are its legs like? | Invisible | Webbed like flippers | Long and thin | *Short and thick
exercise: Which phrase describes a short, chunky pencil? | a silent pencil | a sparkly pencil | *a stumpy pencil
exercise: In «Tardigrades have 8 stumpy legs ending in claws», find and copy the word that means short and thick. | claws | *stumpy | ending | legs
test: What does stumpy mean? | Shiny and smooth | *Short and thick | Very tall and thin | Bright red
test: Which word means more short and thick than stumpy? | stumper | stumpiest and tallest | *stumpier | stumps
exam: In «a caterpillar has six true legs at the front, and its stumpy back legs are fleshy grippers», what does stumpy mean? | *Short and thick | Hairy and wet | Pointed and sharp | Long and bendy
